---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import {
  QuestionnaireControlled,
  QuestionnairePlayground,
  QuestionnaireShortcuts,
  QuestionnaireSizes,
  QuestionnaireStates,
} from "../../components/QuestionnaireDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Questionnaire"
  description="A form that asks one question at a time, with choices or a typed answer, Skip for optional questions, and Submit on the last one."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Questionnaire</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A form that asks one question at a time. Each item holds radio or checkbox
    choices, or a typed answer. Next checks required answers, Skip clears
    optional ones, and the last item submits the form.
  </p>
  <div id="questionnaire-demo">
    <div class="mt-8"><QuestionnairePlayground client:load /></div>
    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="tsx"
        title="A three-step questionnaire"
        code={`import {
  Questionnaire,
  QuestionnaireActions,
  QuestionnaireChoice,
  QuestionnaireChoiceDescription,
  QuestionnaireChoices,
  QuestionnaireDescription,
  QuestionnaireError,
  QuestionnaireInput,
  QuestionnaireItem,
  QuestionnaireNext,
  QuestionnairePrevious,
  QuestionnaireProgress,
  QuestionnaireSkip,
  QuestionnaireSubmit,
  QuestionnaireTitle,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/questionnaire";

<Questionnaire
  items={[
    { name: "style", required: true, choices: [{ value: "short" }, { value: "detailed" }] },
    { name: "plants", choices: [{ value: "tulips" }, { value: "daisies" }] },
    { name: "note" },
  ]}
  onSubmit={(event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    save(new FormData(event.currentTarget));
  }}
>
  <QuestionnaireProgress />
  <QuestionnaireItem name="style" required>
    <QuestionnaireTitle>How should answers look?</QuestionnaireTitle>
    <QuestionnaireDescription>Pick one reply style.</QuestionnaireDescription>
    <QuestionnaireChoices>
      <QuestionnaireChoice value="short">
        Short answers
        <QuestionnaireChoiceDescription>A quick summary.</QuestionnaireChoiceDescription>
      </QuestionnaireChoice>
      <QuestionnaireChoice value="detailed">Detailed answers</QuestionnaireChoice>
    </QuestionnaireChoices>
    <QuestionnaireError>Choose a reply style.</QuestionnaireError>
  </QuestionnaireItem>
  <QuestionnaireItem name="plants" multiple>…</QuestionnaireItem>
  <QuestionnaireItem name="note">
    <QuestionnaireTitle>Anything else?</QuestionnaireTitle>
    <QuestionnaireInput aria-label="Additional note" value={note} onChange={…} />
  </QuestionnaireItem>
  <QuestionnaireActions>
    <QuestionnairePrevious />
    <QuestionnaireSkip />
    <QuestionnaireNext />
    <QuestionnaireSubmit />
  </QuestionnaireActions>
  <Button type="reset" variant="outline">Restart</Button>
</Questionnaire>`}
      />
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>Questionnaire</code>: a <code>form</code>. <code>items</code>
          sets the step order and choice shortcuts; without it, rendered items are
          used in order. <code>defaultItem</code>, or <code>item</code>
          with <code>onItemChange</code>, picks the shown step. A
          <code>reset</code> clears answers and returns to the first step.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>QuestionnaireItem</code>: one question, a
          <code>fieldset</code>. <code>required</code> hides Skip,
          <code>multiple</code> uses checkboxes, <code>disabled</code> drops it from
          the steps, <code>invalid</code> forces the error, and
          <code>onStatusChange</code> reports <code>unanswered</code>,
          <code>answered</code>, or <code>skipped</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>QuestionnaireChoice</code>: <code>value</code>, plus
          <code>defaultChecked</code> or <code>checked</code>,
          <code>disabled</code>, and <code>onChange</code>.
          <code>QuestionnaireChoiceDescription</code> adds a muted line.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>QuestionnaireInput</code>: a typed answer (<code>text</code>,
          <code>email</code>, <code>number</code>, <code>date</code>, and more).
          It is sent with the form only while it has text.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>QuestionnaireError</code>: hidden until someone tries to move on
          without an answer. Its default text depends on
          <code>required</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>QuestionnairePrevious</code>, <code>QuestionnaireSkip</code>,
          <code>QuestionnaireNext</code>, <code>QuestionnaireSubmit</code>: each
          shows only when it applies. They take Button
          <code>size</code> and <code>variant</code>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
      <p>
        <code>shortcuts="letters"</code> or <code>"numbers"</code> shows a key on
        each enabled choice. With <code>items</code>, keys follow its order and
        skip disabled choices.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4"><QuestionnaireShortcuts client:load /></div>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
      <p>
        A required item shows its error and stays put until answered. A disabled
        item is left out of the count. Skipping an optional last question
        submits the form.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4"><QuestionnaireStates client:load /></div>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Action sizes</h2>
      <p>
        By default Previous and Skip are <code>outline</code> and Next and Submit
        are <code>default</code>, at the <code>default</code> size. Inside a dense
        chat reply, <code>sm</code> with <code>ghost</code>
        back buttons fits better.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4"><QuestionnaireSizes client:load /></div>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Controlled step</h2>
      <p>
        Pass <code>item</code> and <code>onItemChange</code> to keep the step in your
        own state. Focus moves to the shown item when it changes.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4"><QuestionnaireControlled client:load /></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Each item is a <code>fieldset</code> named by its <code>legend</code>
      title and described by its description and, while shown, its error (<code
        >role="alert"</code
      >). Hidden items and buttons are
      <code>inert</code>. Progress is a <code>progressbar</code> that announces "Question
      2 of 3".
    </p>
    <p>
      Keys: <kbd>↑</kbd>
      <kbd>↓</kbd> move between answers, <kbd>Enter</kbd>
      on an answer moves on, <kbd>⌘</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Enter</kbd>
      moves on from anywhere, and <kbd>←</kbd>
      <kbd>→</kbd> go back or forward outside text fields. Each control lists its
      keys in
      <code>aria-keyshortcuts</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The shown item fades in over 160ms and marks pop in over 140ms; with
      reduced motion both change at once. Rows are 44px tall, and on phones
      buttons and the text field are too.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Rows use <code>--sprout-input</code> borders, and a picked row uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code> and <code>--sprout-primary-subtle</code>
      with a <code>--sprout-primary</code> mark. Errors use
      <code>--sprout-danger</code>; help text uses
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
